    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.cursorword\n\n### Description\n\nI want to disable mini.cursorword in visual mode. I have used the following snippet, it disables/enables only after moving cursor in Visual mode.\n\n```lua\n-- disable minicursorword when in Visual mode\nautocmd(\"ModeChanged\", {\n  pattern = \"*:[vV\\x16]\",  -- v: character-wise, V: line-wise, Ctrl-V: block-wise\n  callback = function()\n    vim.b.minicursorword_disable = true\n  end,\n})\nautocmd(\"ModeChanged\", {\n  pattern = \"[vV\\x16]:*\",  -- From Visual modes to any other mode\n  callback = function()\n    vim.b.minicursorword_disable = false\n  end,\n})\n```\n\nI see that in module, there are internal APIs used to achive enable/disable for Insert mode. Would it be possible to expose those APIs to user? https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/1fdbb864e2015eb6f501394d593630f825154385/lua/mini/cursorword.lua#L155-L156",
