            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nAlthough I understand the use case, I'd rather not export extra functionality for use cases that are not really common *but* if there is a reasonable workaround. Luckily, there is here: creating these autocommands *before* calling `setup()` leads to unhighlighting right away. This is because those autocommands will be executed before the 'ModeChanged' one created by `require('mini.cursorword').setup()` (because they were created earlier; this is currently how autocommand order works).\n\nAnother approach is to add `vim.api.nvim_exec_autocmds('CursorMoved', {})` inside both autocommands to force recomputation.\n\nClosing as \"working as intended but I understand that it might be better, sorry\".\n\n---\n\nJust in case, for future self: there *is* a way to make these autocommands work as is with the following patch:\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/lua/mini/cursorword.lua b/lua/mini/cursorword.lua\nindex b83e139a..1b50c198 100644\n--- a/lua/mini/cursorword.lua\n+++ b/lua/mini/cursorword.lua\n@@ -162,8 +162,8 @@ H.create_autocommands = function()\n   end\n \n   au('CursorMoved', '*', H.auto_highlight, 'Auto highlight cursorword')\n-  au({ 'InsertEnter', 'TermEnter', 'QuitPre' }, '*', H.auto_unhighlight, 'Auto unhighlight cursorword')\n-  au('ModeChanged', '*:[^i]', H.auto_highlight, 'Auto highlight cursorword')\n+  au({ 'QuitPre' }, '*', H.auto_unhighlight, 'Auto unhighlight cursorword')\n+  au('ModeChanged', '*:*', H.auto_highlight, 'Auto highlight cursorword')\n \n   au('ColorScheme', '*', H.create_default_hl, 'Ensure colors')\n   au('FileType', 'TelescopePrompt', function() vim.b.minicursorword_disable = true end, 'Disable locally')\n@@ -281,7 +281,10 @@ H.unhighlight = function(only_current)\n   end\n end\n \n-H.should_highlight = function() return not H.is_disabled() and H.is_cursor_on_keyword() end\n+H.should_highlight = function()\n+  local mode = vim.fn.mode()\n+  return not H.is_disabled() and H.is_cursor_on_keyword() and not (mode == 'i' or mode == 't')\n+end\n \n -- Utilities ------------------------------------------------------------------\n H.error = function(msg) error('(mini.cursorword) ' .. msg, 0) end\n```\n\nThe problem here is that it introduces `vim.fn.mode()` call for *every* `ModeChanged` event. Which is better avoided if not absolutely needed.",
